<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27395" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyrĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		lyra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the lute</i> or <i>lyre, lyric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyrici soni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 94</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 1, 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Anacreon</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 2, 364</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regnator lyricae cohortis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Pindar</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 7, 5</span></i>
			.— Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyrĭca</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>lyric poems</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 7, 17, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 1,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyrĭcus</span></b> ,
				i, 
			
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυρικο:ς</span>, <i>a lyric poet</i>, <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep.
				4, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bacchylides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 25, 4, 3</span></i>
			.—Usually plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyrĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>lyric poets</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 8, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 6, 71</span></i>; 10, 1, 96;
			61 (in <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 55</span></i>, written in Gr. letters,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυρικοί</span>).</div>
